This covers the Kotlin, the C bridge, the build, the tests and the patches in
this repository, and nothing else.

It does not cover the engine under native/openevv. That is openevv's own work
under its own MIT licence, and it is fetched from upstream rather than copied
in here.

It does not cover the language data that engine carries. That is transcribed
from IBM's Embedded ViaVoice objects and is IBM's; native/openevv/NOTICE says
what it is, whose it is, and who the rights in it may belong to today. Nobody
here is in a position to license it to anyone.

No pronunciation dictionary is included. The ones worth loading belong to the
people who wrote them, and the best known collection carries no licence at all,
so it is linked rather than copied and the test fixture here is written for the
purpose.
